    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0307" n="295" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg295"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">870.811/234: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gunther</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-03T19:00:00+02:00">March 3, 1941—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 4—3:06 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>220. My 174, February 22, noon.<anchor n="58" xml:id="d309-f1"/> The Secretary
                    General of the Foreign Office informs me that the only important development at
                    the recent Vienna Danubian meeting was the admission of Russia on the commission
                    which hereafter will deal with the Upper Danube.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gunther</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
